    "title": "Third 7Brew location in the city set for construction this fall",
    "text": "Work on a 7Brew coffee shop is set to begin this fall, as indicated in a filing with a state regulatory agency.\nAccording to the filing, the $750,000 project will involve constructing a 510 square-foot drive-thru only coffee shop. The project, located at 6407 W. U.S. Hwy. 158, is expected to start on November 10 and be completed by December 17. It is noted that construction timelines on state filings are often preliminary and subject to change.\nCoy Haynes, a co-founding partner at Dallas-based Laramie Investments, is developing the project under the subsidiary CG 191 and 158 LLC. The design firm Arkifex Studios from Springfield, Missouri, managed the archetypal aspects of the project.\nAccording to the 7Brew website, there are two locations in Midland. One is located at 2201 W. Texas Avenue and the other is situated at 3316 W. Loop 250 N.",
